## 9. sheet_id Passthrough Chain

Client Config's `Sheet ID` existed in schema but was never read into the MRA payload. Added at Step 5, threaded through every Code Node that **explicitly reconstructs its return object**: Steps 7, 7b, 9, 10a, 11, 12, 13, 14, 16a.

**Node classification pattern established here (reusable for any future field addition):**
- **Fetch/HTTP nodes** — no passthrough needed; they don't rebuild payloads.
- **Non-rebuilding IF/Switch nodes** — pass the item through unchanged; no code change needed.
- **Code Nodes that reconstruct their return object key-by-key** — any field not explicitly listed is silently dropped. This is the category that needs the one-line addition at each hop.

Walk any future field addition through this same three-way classification before assuming it "just carries through."

---

## 10. Multi-Recipient Email

**Prior documented claim (now confirmed false):** "Brevo auto-parses comma-separated addresses." Direct code read showed the entire raw string was placed into a single recipient object's `email` field — no split logic existed.

**Fix, applied to 17a/17b/17c:**
```javascript
const raw_emails = s16.approval_email || 'miguel@solofella.com';
const email_list = raw_emails.split(/[,;]/).map(e => e.trim()).filter(e => e.length > 0);
const brevo_to_arr = [];
for (let i = 0; i < email_list.length; i++) {
  const recipient = {};
  recipient['email'] = email_list[i];
  recipient['name'] = client_name;
  brevo_to_arr.push(recipient);
}
```

Required Client Config's Approval Contact Email field type change: NocoDB `Email` (single-address validated) → `LongText`.

**Real production confirmation:** AJI-005's daily email showed two real client addresses plus `miguel@solofella.com` CC'd — confirmed intentional internal oversight, not a bug displacing real recipients. This resolves the earlier Sheet-Sync/RDA email ambiguity.

**Unresolved, not a defect:** if Approval Contact Email is blank, code defaults to `miguel@solofella.com`. Whether that's the intended long-term fallback (vs. erroring/skipping) has not been decided.

---

## 11. Sheet URL Fix (17a/17b only)

Both nodes previously contained an identical hardcoded literal pointing to **PAK-001's own Google Sheet** — every client, including all 5 AJI locations, received PAK-001's link.

**Fix:**
```javascript
const sheet_id = s16.sheet_id || '';
const sheet_url = 'https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/' + sheet_id + '/edit';
```

**17c requires no fix** — confirmed by direct code read that this node only links to `dashboard_url` (already dynamic), never to a Sheet.

**Separate non-code fix required:** each client's Google Sheet document needed its own Drive sharing setting changed to "Anyone with the link" — otherwise recipients hit a Google access-request wall regardless of correct URL routing. Confirmed resolved via live test.

