## 13. Magic Link Token & Dashboard Access

Generated at Step 12 using `Math.random()` — **not a CSPRNG**, despite functioning as a real access-control credential embedded in live client dashboard URLs (`https://subtextcx.solofella.com/{client_id}?token=...`, 72hr expiry). Flagged as a security-relevant gap; no fix applied yet (Diagnose-Only Rule — awaiting explicit request).

---

## 14. Delivery Tracking

Step 19 marks `Delivery Status: "sent"` **unconditionally**, without checking Step 18's actual Brevo response for success. A hard network failure would still throw via n8n's default behavior, but a softer failure (bad recipient, Brevo-level rejection) would not be caught. Same observability gap as SIA's unverified bulk write — no agent in the pipeline currently verifies MRA's or SIA's writes the way ALA/EIP/ESS/HSI/BRA/RDA verify theirs via a "Capture Record ID, throw if missing" step. Step 16a is the one exception in MRA itself — it does correctly implement throw-if-no-ID.

