## 15. Consolidated Known Issues (all open, none actioned)

🔴 **Critical / safety-relevant:**
1. Daily-report signal classification silently drops Dignity-Risk and two other real Signal Type values (§7).
2. Dead `Published`-status dependency zeroes SLA compliance, response velocity, and all SEO metrics permanently, every report (§8).
3. Hardcoded fabricated "100% Response Coverage" in weekly email (§12).
4. Magic Link Token uses `Math.random()`, not a CSPRNG, for a real access credential (§13).

🟡 **Functional but silent:**
5. Trend-arrow logic checks wrong enum values, never displays real trend direction (§12).
6. Delivery status marked "sent" without checking Brevo's actual response (§14).
7. SEO keyword-hit logic re-scans raw draft text instead of reading RDA's own persisted `SEO Keywords Used` field — this would also sidestep issue #2's dependency chain.

⚪ **Cosmetic / low-risk:**
8. Step 7's misleading name (no-op, but harmless — Step 9 does the real work).
9. Daily email subject singular/plural ("1 reviews").
10. Sender name casing inconsistency.

⚪ **Unresolved design questions, not defects:**
11. MRA monthly calendar-month window vs. SIA's rolling-30-day window — mismatch not reconciled.
12. Step 9's midnight-reset of period_end excluding the final day of each period — intent unconfirmed.
13. Fallback-to-miguel@solofella.com when Approval Contact Email is blank — intended or not, undecided.
14. One-hour schedule stagger after SIA's corresponding triggers — likely deliberate dependency ordering, not independently confirmed.

⚪ **Scalability, lower urgency (single-client-scoped, unlike SIA's cross-client version of the same risk):**
15. Steps 6, 10c, 10d use hardcoded `limit=1000` with no server-side date filter or confirmed sort order — same latent risk pattern flagged in SIA's audit.

