## 16. Locked Lessons Carried Forward

1. Filter by ALA Date, never RDA Timestamp.
2. Step 11's conditional source must use named references, never `$input`.
3. `filtered_ala_record_ids` built at Step 9, consumed at Step 11's daily branch.
4. Always `String()`-wrap ALA Record ID before comparison — type mismatches are silent.
5. Loop-back node must produce exactly one item unconditionally every iteration — not "last node in chain."
6. Field passthrough requires per-node classification (fetch/HTTP vs. non-rebuilding IF vs. reconstructing Code Node) — never assume automatic carry-through.
7. NocoDB field *type* constrains multi-value data — Email type ≠ multi-address capable; use LongText.
8. Google Sheet sharing settings are independent of correct URL routing — a Drive permission, not fixable in workflow code.
9. Blank source data silently distorts averages without any visible error — check data completeness before assuming a calculation defect.
10. `records[0]`-only patterns silently truncate multi-row fetches to one row with zero errors — worth auditing any other agent that bulk-fetches Client Config or similar shared tables.

